.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH lrat 1  lrat 
.SH NAME
lrat \- A fast, keyboard\-first terminal client for Linear
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlrat\fR [\fB\-\-demo\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A fast, keyboard\-first terminal client for Linear
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-demo\fR
Run without a Linear account or API key
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
lrat\-auth(1)
Manage the Linear API key
.TP
lrat\-completions(1)
Print the completion script for a shell
.TP
lrat\-open(1)
Open an issue\*(Aqs Linear page in the browser
.TP
lrat\-doctor(1)
Check the API key, Linear, the terminal, the config and the version
.SH EXTRA
Getting started:
  lrat auth login    store a Linear API key in the keyring (see `lrat auth \-\-help`)
  lrat               open My Issues
  lrat \-\-demo        try lrat without an account

LINEAR_API_KEY, when set, is used instead of the keyring.
